From bec105e9b3cfaa593e4fb32c8b96932ab16d3725 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: deten <6029514+deten@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:58:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] egl: forward EGL_KHR_fence_sync and EGL_KHR_wait_sync
 properly

The sync calls went through the generic dynamic dispatch, which passed
the stub's display index as the EGLDisplay and the client's 64-bit
attribute-list pointer through unchanged. eglCreateSyncKHR therefore
failed (or read unrelated memory), and a client that synchronises
contexts with EGL fences (WebKit: painting threads to compositor) got no
synchronisation at all.

eglCreateSyncKHR, eglDestroySyncKHR, eglClientWaitSyncKHR, eglWaitSyncKHR
and eglGetSyncAttribKHR now have their own opcodes: the display index is
translated, the attribute list copied, the sync handle passed back as an
opaque value.

Fence waits in the single-threaded proxy: a client wait blocks every
context until the fence signals, which is only safe if the fence's
commands have been submitted. The proxy flushes right after creating a
fence and adds EGL_SYNC_FLUSH_COMMANDS_BIT_KHR to client waits, so the
GPU always makes progress and the wait ends on its own; server waits
(eglWaitSyncKHR) never block the proxy.
---
 include/gles_bridge_protocol.h |   7 +++
 proxy/protocol/egl.c           |  96 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 proxy/protocol/egl.h           |   5 ++
 proxy/proxy.c                  |   5 ++
 stub/egl_stub.c                | 109 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 222 insertions(+)

